<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36782" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Poeas</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paeas</span></b> ), antis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ποίας</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the father of Philoctetes</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 9,
				233</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Oet. 1603</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				14</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Poeantĭădes</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paeant-</span></b> ), ae,
				m., <i>the son of Pœas</i>,
			i. e. <i>Philoctetes</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13,
				313</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Poeantĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paeant-</span></b> ), a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Pœas</i>, <i>Pœantian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Poeantia proles,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Philoctetes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					13, 45</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">also: heros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. R. Am. 111</span></i>
			; and <i>absol.</i> Poeantius, <i><span class="en">id. Tr. 5,
				1, 61</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
